Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:02:56 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?gpu:=20M1.0.5=20=E2=80=94=20the=20Metal=20prese?=
 =?UTF-8?q?nt=20moves=20to=20its=20own=20thread?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

the real game showed the presenter eating the emulation's budget:
85% of the frame loop slept inside nextDrawable waiting for the
display's vsync, on the same thread the software raster runs on —
MM3D fell from 54 fps to 26. The whole Metal bundle (device, queue,
layer, pipeline, textures) now lives on a dedicated worker thread;
the app's thread clones the frame's pixels (~7 MB, about a
millisecond) and hands them over through a one-frame channel, so
the raster and the wait for the drawable overlap instead of
queueing. the layout settings ride an Arc<Mutex> snapshot, the
window's size is stamped on each job and only re-applied when it
actually changed (the off-main setDrawableSize would make Core
Animation re-prepare the drawables every frame), and two texture
sets ping-pong so an upload never races the previous job's draw.

the game's flame after this lands clean: the main thread now waits
inside the rayon fill of the software raster itself — the present
is off the budget, and what remains is exactly the wall the M1.1
HardwareMetal port takes down. the test pattern composes exactly;
native_smoke 7/7.
